{
  "description": "Negative conformance vectors for the A/B fallback update contract v0.1. Each document MUST FAIL validation against its schema for the stated reason; tools/validate_ab_update_examples.py enforces this and fails the build if any of them validates. Every case is otherwise complete, so a failure is attributable to the named defect rather than to a missing required field. The vectors encode the failure modes that make an update irreversible: writing the slot you fall back to, settling on the slot that failed, promoting through a gate that cannot fail, an unbootable slot the selector will still pick, and a watchdog pair with only one kind in it.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "schema": "UpdateTransaction.json",
